# The held weapon art is third-party CC-BY work (see ASSET-LICENSES.md). It is prepared locally
# and never committed: the two runtime GLBs plus their sources run to hundreds of megabytes,
# against a repository whose entire history is tens. What IS committed is everything needed to
# reproduce them -- the attribution, the provenance and the preparation scripts under prepare/.
#
# Keeping the art out is what makes the build conditional: see the BLOCK_HAVE_VIEWMODEL_ART
# branch in ../../CMakeLists.txt, which is why a clean clone still configures, builds and plays.
/source/
/source-textures/
/prepared-textures/
*.glb
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.ktx2

# Blender/python scratch from running prepare/ in place.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
